<title>INDIA: TABLE-India's Bata India 6-mth net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-India's Bata India 6-mth net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		83.5     vs	1.5</p>
<p>    Net sales	    3,418.9     vs  2,920.0</p>
<p>    Other income	    12.2     vs	1.6</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  3,205.4     vs  2,771.4</p>
<p>    Interest		  82.1     vs    100.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    60.1     vs     48.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 nil	vs	nil</p>
<p>Note: Bata India, a leading shoe-maker, attributed the turnaround in its performance to a marketing strategy, which emphasises the introduction of low to medium price footwear at popular prices, combined with restructuring measures and cost reductions.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
